'''''Lanterns''''' is an American [[Superhero fiction|superhero]] television series created by Chris Mundy, [[Damon Lindelof]], and [[Tom King (writer)|Tom King]] for [[HBO]], based on the [[DC Comics]] [[Green Lantern]] characters [[Hal Jordan]] and [[John Stewart (character)|John Stewart]]. It is the third television series in the [[DC Universe (franchise)|DC Universe]] (DCU). It features experienced Lantern Hal Jordan and new recruit John Stewart as they team up with local sheriff Kerry Kane to investigate murders in [[Rushville, Nebraska]] that leads to a wider mystery. The series was produced by [[DC Studios]] and [[Warner Bros. Television]] with Mundy serving as showrunner.

[[Kyle Chandler]], [[Aaron Pierre (actor)|Aaron Pierre]] and [[Kelly Macdonald]] respectively star as Jordan, Stewart and Kane. [[Garret Dillahunt]], [[Poorna Jagannathan]] and [[Ulrich Thomsen]] also star. [[Greg Berlanti]] began developing a Green Lantern television series by October 2019. After [[James Gunn]] and [[Peter Safran]] became co-CEOs of DC Studios in October 2022, the series was redeveloped. It was announced in January 2023, along with its [[Detective fiction|detective story]] style, which was inspired by the series ''[[True Detective]]'' (2014–present) and ''[[Slow Horses]]'' (2022–present). The involvement of Mundy, Lindelof, and King was confirmed in mid-2024 when HBO ordered the series. ''Slow Horses''{{'s}} [[James Hawes]] was hired to direct the first two episodes in October, when Chandler and Pierre were cast. Filming took place in Los Angeles from February to July 2025, with [[Stephen Williams (director)|Stephen Williams]], [[Geeta Vasant Patel]], and [[Alik Sakharov]] also directing.

''Lanterns'' premiered on August 16, 2026, and ran for eight episodes through October 4. It is part of the DCU's [[Chapter One: Gods and Monsters]]. The series received positive reviews and had strong viewership.

== Premise ==
[[Green Lantern (DC Universe)|Green Lantern]]s are interstellar peacekeepers who wear [[Power ring (DC Universe)|rings]] that give them extraordinary powers. The series follows experienced Lantern [[Hal Jordan (DC Universe)|Hal Jordan]] and new recruit [[John Stewart (DC Universe)|John Stewart]] as they investigate a murder in [[Rushville, Nebraska]], which Hal believes is an extraterrestrial incident and leads them to darker mysteries and reckonings.<ref name="VFFeb2025" /><ref name="EWTimelines" />

== Cast and characters ==
[[File:Lanterns at San Diego Comic Con 2026.jpg|thumb|alt=Picture of the ''Lanterns'' panel featuring Chris Mundy, Aaron Pierre, Kyle Chandler, Damon Lindelof, Poorna Jagannathan, Garret Dillahunt, Tom King, and Nathan Fillion at San Diego Comic Con 2026|Showrunner Chris Mundy, stars Aaron Pierre and Kyle Chandler, co-creator Damon Lindelof, co-stars Poorna Jagannathan and Garret Dillahunt, co-creator Tom King, and guest star Nathan Fillion promoting ''Lanterns'' at the 2026 San Diego Comic-Con]]

=== Main ===
* [[Kyle Chandler]] as [[Hal Jordan (DC Universe)|Hal Jordan / Green Lantern]]:<br/>A [[United States Air Force|USAF]] veteran, former test pilot, and legendary member of the [[Green Lantern Corps (DC Universe)|Green Lantern Corps]],<ref name="VFFeb2025" /><ref name="ChandlerCast" /> who is responsible for protecting Sector 2814.<ref name="Ep1SurpriseEnding" /> In the series, Hal is approaching retirement,<ref name="VFFeb2025" /><ref name="ChandlerCast" /> and is filling in to train John Stewart.<ref name="SãoPauloUpfront" /> The [[Guardians of the Universe (DC Universe)|Guardians of the Universe]], who founded and lead the Corps, are concerned about what Hal may or may not have inherited from his former mentor Thaal Sinestro.<ref name="EWJul2026" /> The writers took inspiration for the character from [[Sam Shepard]]'s portrayal of [[Chuck Yeager]] in the film ''[[The Right Stuff (film)|The Right Stuff]]'' (1983). [[Showrunner]] Chris Mundy felt Chandler had the same qualities as well as a "dry wit" they felt was important for Hal.<ref name="VFFeb2025" /> Henry Samiri portrays a young Hal in [[Flashback (narrative)|flashback]] scenes.<ref name="Ep7RecapDecider" />
* [[Aaron Pierre (actor)|Aaron Pierre]] as [[John Stewart (DC Universe)|John Stewart]]:<br/>A new [[Green Lantern (DC Universe)|Green Lantern]] recruit whom Hal is training to replace himself.<ref name="VFFeb2025" /><ref name="PierreCast" /> John is considered an anomaly because he is the first Green Lantern in the Corps' history to have been recruited by the Guardians of the Universe instead of being chosen by a [[Power ring (DC Universe)|power ring]], as is customary.<ref name="EWTimelines" /> Mundy said the character was both a [[United States Marine Corps|Marine]] and an artistic architect,<ref name="PierreOct2025MH" /><ref name="HawesApr2025" /> and felt Pierre could portray both of these aspects. He said Pierre was a "serious theater actor, yet he also looks like he was built in a lab to be an action star".<ref name="VFFeb2025" /> Director [[James Hawes]] said Pierre had "a magnificent presence. He feels so forceful, so cool, so understated."<ref name="HawesApr2025" /> Jayce Eiland and Cairo Cash Lee portray John as a child and a teenager, respectively, in flashback scenes.<ref name="CashLee" /><ref name="Ep3ReviewDoG" />
* [[Kelly Macdonald]] as Kerry Kane: The sheriff of [[Rushville, Nebraska]], who originally hailed from [[Gotham City (DC Universe)|Gotham City]].<ref name="GothamCityConnection" /><ref name="Macdonald" /> Kerry is deeply devoted to her family and close-knit town,<ref name="EWTimelines" /> while also territorial around Hal and John upon their arrival at Rushville.<ref name="TeaserTrailerRemovalEW" /> Kerry is a love interest for Hal in the series.<ref name="FirstLookDeadline" />
* [[Garret Dillahunt]] as William "Will" Macon: Kerry's father-in-law and a powerful rancher whose avowed aim is to protect his community from alien threats<ref name="Dillahunt" />
* [[Poorna Jagannathan]] as Zoe Macon: A [[Manhunters (DC Comics)|Manhunter]] posing as William's human wife who seduces John to gain his trust<ref name="TeaserTrailerRemovalEW" /><ref name="JagannathanEWSep2026" />
* [[Ulrich Thomsen]] as [[Sinestro (DC Universe)|Thaal Sinestro]]: A "ruthless yet undeniably charming" former Green Lantern, and Hal's mentor and father figure,<ref name="Thomsen" /><ref name="SinestroHannibalLecter" /> who went rogue and was expelled from the Green Lantern Corps after a failed [[coup]],<ref name="EWJul2026" /> during which he killed one of the twelve Guardians of the Universe.<ref name="Ep3RecapDecider" /> Sinestro appears imprisoned in space as of 2016,<ref name="NewTrailerDeadline" /> though he had escaped by 2026.<ref name="Ep6RecapTR" />

=== Recurring ===
* [[Jason Ritter]] as Billy Macon: Kerry's lawyer husband and William's son who does his father's bidding.<ref name="Ritter" /><ref name="Ritter2" /> Several years following the events of 2016, Billy and Kerry have divorced.<ref name="NYTEp6Recap" />
* [[J. Alphonse Nicholson]] as John Stewart Sr.: John's father who is in the military<ref name="Nicholson" />
* [[Cary Christopher]] and Shea Pritchard as Noah Macon: Kerry and Billy's son and William's grandson who is later revealed to be a Manhunter. Christopher portrays Noah as a child in 2016 while Pritchard portrays Noah as a teenager in 2026.<ref name="Christopher" /><ref name="NYTEp6Recap" />
* Michael Ocampo as Lopez: A deputy with the Rushville police<ref name="OcampoBrown" />
* [[Paul Ben-Victor]] as Antaan: An extraterrestrial leader who seeks revenge for the [[genocide]] of his species and possesses the ability to detonate his body<ref name="Ben-Victor" />
* [[Laura Linney]] as [[Lianna (comics)|Lianna]]: A member of the Guardians of the Universe who selects John as a potential Lantern recruit<ref name="LinneyLianna" />
* [[Jasmine Cephas Jones]] as Bernadette Stewart: John's mother<ref name="Jones" />
* Jared Grimes as Marcus Stewart: John's older brother. Noah Gibson-Slates and Richard Whitney Gardenhire Jr. portray Marcus respectively as a child and teenager.<ref name="NYTEp6Recap" />
* Romeo Brown as Aaron Stewart: John's older brother. Lumi Oniyide and Jaylen Lyndon Hunter portray Aaron respectively as a child and teenager.<ref name="OcampoBrown" />
* Hannah Christine Shetler as Maggie: A waitress who works at a café in Rushville<ref name="NYTEp6Recap" />

=== Guest ===
* [[Chris Coy]] as "Waylon Sanders": An alien and a member of Antaan's species who disguises himself as a nervous truck driver<ref name="Coy" /><ref name="TrailerSDCC" />
* Sergio Lanza as a Green Lantern recruiter who approaches John in 2016<ref name="Ep3RecapVulture" />
* [[Jason Manuel Olazabal]] as Hector Gutiérrez: An engineer forced by William to pose as [[Hector Hammond]], owner of Atlas Inc., who operates various high-tech slaughterhouses<ref name="Olazabal" />
* [[Nathan Fillion]] as [[Guy Gardner (DC Universe)|Guy Gardner / Green Lantern]]: A former [[physical education]] teacher and abrasive Green Lantern who is a member of the [[Justice Gang]].<ref name="FillionConfirm" /><ref name="EWJul2026" /> Fillion described the character as  "a little bit higher strung" in ''Lanterns'' compared to his introduction in the [[DC Universe (franchise)|DC Universe]] (DCU) film ''[[Superman (2025 film)|Superman]]'' (2025), and that he enjoyed exploring the character in a new environment.<ref name="FillionEWJun2025" />
* Amie MacKenzie as [[Carol Ferris]]: Hal's former love interest<ref name="NYTEp6Recap" />
* Jake B. Miller as [[Martin Jordan]]: Hal's deceased father<ref name="Ep7RecapDecider" />
* [[Matt Rhule]] as a fictional version of himself who is the head coach of the [[Nebraska Cornhuskers football team]]<ref name="Rhule" />

